    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
    # affiliation: "TODO"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Verture-Liu/2026summerproject"
url: "https://verture-liu.github.io/2026summerproject/"
abstract: >-
  PaleoRigor is a local, human-in-the-loop system that converts a natural-language
  research request into an explicit workflow built from predefined analysis
  skills. It validates file references, formats and step compatibility before
  execution, requires expert approval, restricts execution to registered skills,
  and retains final outputs, intermediate files and run records so that the path
  from request to result can be audited. It supports workflow review and
  traceable source-data preparation before specialist paleomicrobiome
  interpretation; it does not authenticate ancient DNA or perform biological
  interpretation.
keywords:
  - paleomicrobiome
  - ancient DNA
  - human-in-the-loop analysis
  - source-data verification
  - reproducible bioinformatics
  - workflow validation
